course: dictionary
lesson: 15298
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. Skinny can describe a thin person or animal, clothes that fit very tightly, or a drink made with low-fat milk. The words around it show you which meaning to use.
explain: «The kitten was so skinny that you could count its ribs.» Here skinny means very thin, sometimes too thin. «Mum bought me new skinny jeans.» Here skinny describes clothes that fit closely. Look at what skinny is describing.
explain: Be kind with this word. Calling a person skinny can hurt their feelings, so think before you say it about someone's body. Skinny also appears in slang: «Tell me the skinny on the school trip» means tell me the facts.
fact: Skinny means very thin, sometimes too thin.
fact: Skinny clothes fit closely, like «skinny jeans».
fact: A «skinny latte» is made with low-fat milk.
fact: In US slang, «the skinny» means the inside information or the facts.
fact: «Skinny dipping» means swimming without any clothes on.
exercise: «The kitten was so skinny that you could count its ribs.» What does skinny mean here? | Very fat | *Very thin | Very loud | Very wet
exercise: Dad orders a «skinny latte» at the café. What does skinny mean in this sentence? | Served in a paper cup | Served very hot | Made with a lot of sugar | *Made with low-fat milk
exercise: «Mum bought me new skinny jeans.» What do skinny jeans do? | Float in water | *Fit closely | Keep you warm in snow | Have big pockets
test: In US slang, what does «the skinny» mean? | A type of noodle | A thin person | A small fish | *The inside information or facts
test: Which sentence uses skinny to mean very thin? | I went skinny dipping in the lake. | I wore my skinny jeans to school. | Tell me the skinny on the trip. | *The skinny kitten crept under the fence.
exam: What does skinny mean in «a skinny latte»? | Very cold | *Made with low-fat milk | Very thin | Made with no milk at all
